web SPA: vite+react19+ts-strict+zustand. every capable browser, capability-gated degradation (src/core/capabilities.ts: chromium/screenCapture/systemAudioCapture/camera/webCodecs/opfs/ios/appleWebKit). Apple WebKit: no tab/system audio; iOS: no screen capture in any browser (native-only — ScreenCaptureKit on iOS 27+, TASKS P5) — UI drops unsupported channels from the effective config; an unusable input renders red (slashed icon), stays clickable, and shows its per-platform reason only on press (channels.ts unsupportedReason) — no persistent notice banner.
src/core = framework-free engine; src/app = react UI (imports @core/* only via module indexes). contracts: src/core/types.ts (authoritative).
code-split (O7): first paint carries the app shell + capture screen only (~221KB). the editor chunk is React.lazy behind app/editorChunk.ts (ONE import() so lazy + prefetch resolve the same chunk) and is prefetched the moment recording starts; session.ts/recovery.ts (which drag mediabunny) load via core/capture/lazy.ts and are WARMED at mount by warmCapturePipeline(), so the record click never waits on a fetch; supabase loads on first cloud use. ENFORCEMENT: the @core/capture barrel must never re-export session/recovery VALUES — that pulls the engine back into first paint.
PWA (P2): manifest + public/sw.js, registered in PRODUCTION ONLY (a worker in front of the dev server serves stale modules). worker touches same-origin GET assets/navigations only; range requests pass through untouched (media elements read files that way).
capture: getDisplayMedia fired FIRST, synchronously inside the record-click gesture (WebKit drops transient activation on any prior await → no picker), granted cam/mic overlap the open picker, ungranted run after it. all channels start together: arm() awaits every device (all prompts answered) then start() activates at one epoch — no late-join, equal lengths. video=MediaRecorder webm on Chromium / mp4(h264+aac) on Apple WebKit (isTypeSupported-picked, '' = UA default; never force unsupported → threw on Safari); audio=AudioWorklet→WebCodecs opus→mediabunny webm on Chromium, MediaRecorder mp4/aac on Apple WebKit (WebCodecs audio path truncates to ~1s on Safari; startOffset=first-sample wall for measured, startCall for MediaRecorder). demux is container-agnostic (compose ALL_FORMATS) so mixed-format takes compose fine. durable OPFS writer worker for MediaRecorder path. recording preview = the editor's 16:9 stage — a live WYSIWYG of the final composition (screen letterboxed, camera PiP), sized/positioned pixel-identical to the editor so the frame doesn't move on hand-off to edit; no full-bleed preview. 30min cap. ?synthetic=1 = generated streams.
store: OPFS blobs (blobStore + SyncAccessHandle durable worker) + IndexedDB metadata (recordingsRepo).
timeline: pure math, unit-tested. channel trims blank (no time shift); global trim = output bounds. MID-TAKE CUTS (F1): EditState.segments is an optional ordered list of kept RECORDING-timeline spans, so output→recording time maps PIECEWISE (outputToRecordingMs; channelSourceTimeAt is built on it, which is why video and the editor preview needed no other change). TWO VIEWS, and the distinction matters: editSegments() is what the editor holds (a split is two adjacent spans, so the marker survives until you delete or drag it) while keptSegments() merges adjacent spans because contiguous material is NOT a cut — that is what keeps a split-with-nothing-deleted on the instant path with no seam fade.
compose: mediabunny + WebCodecs. sample channels per frame -> canvas layout -> encode. mp4 avc+aac, fallback avc+opus, then vp9+opus webm. layout: 1080p30 default; screen letterboxed; cam PiP BR 24%w; audio-only=waveform. audio: Hermite resample to 48kHz, soft-limit, seam-safe 1s chunks, plus a ±3ms fade through zero at every cut join. quality tiers (F7) in compose/quality.ts pick width/height/bitrate; only the default tier keeps the instant packet copy.
exports STREAM TO DISK (O1): compose/scratch.ts muxes through mediabunny StreamTarget into an OPFS scratch file via the positioned durable writer, so the muxer holds ~4MB regardless of length; ExportResult.blob is a disk-backed File re-typed with Blob.slice. BufferTarget remains the fallback. The newest finished scratch is kept (the result blob reads from it) and the previous one dropped.
loudness (O2): measured DURING capture (capture/loudnessAccumulator.ts, fed by measuredAudio's onPcm tap) and stored on Recording.loudness, so export and the editor-open preview skip the probe decode. They fall back to the probe whenever the noise-floor term could decide the makeup — capture measures PCM, export measures the decoded file, and they disagree on p20 below the codec floor.
certification (O8): compose/certify.ts writes a JSON record into the container comment tag of every export — path, output settings, loudness makeup and its source, stalled/missing channels, cut count, CI sync bound.
share: saveToFile + ShareTarget list. cloud: supabase adapter behind CloudProvider iface (google oauth, private bucket, signed URL, quota+ttl); null when env unset. E2EE-compatible: provider never requires plaintext metadata beyond size/name.
analytics: event bus, console dev / noop prod.
UI flow: capture -> editor -> exporting -> share (zustand state machine, no router). editor = framed 16:9 stage + one transport row (back · play · time · scrubber · Export; no top header) over a bottom timeline whose ruler sits beneath the lanes. editor preview = DOM-synced <video>s mirroring compositor layout via timeline fns.
